THE CASE AGAINST THE TARGET:
SRC_001 mischaracterizes the obstruction class: a stable mixed configuration requires only that the cut edges form a matching, not an induced matching. Two cut edges can be connected by a same-colored edge between their endpoints. For example, take cut edges uv and xy with u,x red and v,y blue, and add edge ux; give u and x a third red neighbor, v and y two blue neighbors. Then every vertex has at most one opposite neighbor, so the configuration is locally stable, but the cut edges uv and xy are not induced. This invalidates the claimed 'induced matching' obstruction structure and the associated count of traps.

